          "question": "What is osteoarthritis, and is it the same thing as arthritis?",
          "answer": "The search results don't clearly define osteoarthritis or explain how it relates to arthritis in general. The one relevant passage, from the Osteoarthritis reference, mostly covers management and when to seek assessment.\n\n- **Management:** The passage says education, pacing, suitable footwear, walking aids, and heat or cold can help. Medicines are described as supporting options, and joint replacement is considered when pain and limitation continue despite other treatment.\n- **Contrast with other joint conditions:** It distinguishes osteoarthritis from \"inflammatory arthritis,\" which it says is suggested by prolonged morning stiffness, several small joints affected on both sides of the body, or whole-body symptoms. This implies that arthritis covers more than one type of joint problem, but the passage does not list the types.\n\n**Seek prompt care if** a joint is hot, swollen, and very painful, especially with fever. The passage says this needs urgent assessment and is not an osteoarthritis flare. Sudden locking or giving way of a joint, or new nerve symptoms with back or neck pain, also warrant prompt assessment.\n\nThese results don't cover the cause of osteoarthritis, its symptoms in detail, or the full range of arthritis conditions. A clinician or a dedicated patient resource can answer those questions.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
